-- title:
--   Every completed observation count is bounded by the sample cap
-- statement:
--   Let $n,r\in\mathbb N$, and let $o_1,o_2$ be arbitrary Boolean independence-query functions on subsets of $[n]=\{0,\ldots,n-1\}$. Let $t:\mathbb N\to\{0,1\}$ be any tape, $s$ any schedule with $N=s.\mathrm{observations}$, $q\in\mathbb Q$, and $w$ any rational multipliers on distinct ordered pairs in $[n]$. Let $(S,c)$ be any starting paired state and tape cursor. If $\operatorname{observePhase}(r,o_1,o_2,t,s,q,w,(S,c))$ succeeds with observation cursor $o$, then
--   $$\forall a,\qquad o.\mathrm{counts}(a)\le N,$$
--   where $a$ ranges over transversal, defect, and invalid kind labels. This bounds the counters that later appear in rational weight updates.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/PhaseResourcePrimitives.lean#L80-L134

